  51:     """Repeat the teal-like 3x3 sprite once for each singleton marker pixel.
  52: 
  53:     Input structure
  54:     - The grid has a dominant background, one non-background color forming isolated singleton markers, and one other non-background color forming a single 8-connected sprite.
  55:     - The sprite fits inside a unique centroid-centered 3x3 window.
  56: 
  57:     Rule
  58:     - Extract that 3x3 sprite window with background in its empty cells.
  59:     - Concatenate one copy of the sprite window horizontally for each singleton marker.
  60: 
  61:     Key insight
  62:     - The marker pixels encode only the repetition count; the multi-pixel object is the repeated sprite template.
  63:     """
